Subject-perspective review saved to `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Zach-Bryan/2026-08-30_020003/subject.md` (SHA verified against context.json and the supplied argument).

**Verdict:** revise — trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit. **1 blocker, 6 concerns.**

**Strongest hit (SUBJECT-H1/H2):** the draft would be recognizable to Bryan himself — it's built from his own verbatim voice (the Master Chief bottle frame, "It's hard to tell," "I'd rather not"), and it resolves his structure-craving/structure-defying paradox without pathologizing him or excusing the costs.

**Blocker (SUBJECT-R1):** the Springsteen scene is a composite. "A real guilt" and "Why the fuck am I on stage?" are verbatim from the 2023 Rogan interview (Rogan is the one who answers them), but the draft stages them as a confession made to Springsteen in 2024 — and two of the four Springsteen quotes in that scene rest on an unverifiable locator. Repair is surgical: rebuild the scene from the two verified quotes and move the guilt material back to its real setting.

**Highest-priority concern (SUBJECT-R2):** the sentence "her testimony describes exactly what this pattern can feel like from close range" conscripts LaPaglia's unadjudicated account as corroboration of the article's psychological thesis — the one place the draft's fairness discipline slips. Dropping "exactly" and recasting to conditional weight fixes it while keeping the file unsoftened.

One research note in the draft's favor: I verified his November 2025 sobriety post does say "I went out of my way to find a therapist," so the therapy claim I suspected of overreach is grounded — and the same post's "debilitating panic attacks and anxiety" is a stronger on-thesis quote the draft could add (SUBJECT-I1).

Sources: [KGNS coverage of the sobriety post](https://www.kgns.tv/2025/11/20/i-feel-great-zach-bryan-reveals-hes-been-sober-2-months-amid-mental-health-struggles/), [iHeart syndication](https://us1035.iheart.com/content/2025-11-19-zach-bryan-opens-up-about-his-sobriety-mental-health-in-vulnerable-post/)
